'''Neal Scanlan''' (born around [[1960s#1961|1961]]) is a [[Wikipedia:Special effect|special effects artist]] who served as creature effects supervisor on [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'']] and the stand-alone film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''. He is serving as creatures and droids FX on [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker'']]. Scanlan received an [[Wikipedia:Academy Awards|Oscar]] nomination for his work on ''Star Wars: The Force Awakens''.

==Biography==
===''Rogue One: A Star Wars Story''===
Neal Scanlan was the Creature Effects Supervisor for the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[Star Wars Anthology Series|anthology]] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> When [[Pablo Hidalgo]] was writing the reference book ''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]'', he talked to Scanlan to learn what the crew's inspirations for the characters were. When Hidalgo visited the ''Rogue One'' set, he received a crash-course in the [[alien]]s from Scanlan.<ref name="Much to Learn">{{SW|url=news/much-to-learn-you-still-have-talking-rogue-one-aliens-with-pablo-hidalgo|text=Much to Learn You Still Have: Talking ''Rogue One'' Aliens with Pablo Hidalgo}}</ref>

===''Andor'' television series===
{{Quote|We treat this exactly like we would a film, there is no difference in our approach.|Neal Scanlan|<ref name="Sizzle">{{SWYouTube|gSW-pARyP-M|Sizzle Reel &#124; Andor &#124; Disney+|sw_url=video/sizzle-andor}}</ref>}}
[[File:B2EMOPropSDCC.jpg|thumb|left|200px|B2EMO was designed by Neal Scanlan.]]
Neal Scanlan was the Creature and Droid FX Creative Supervisor for the ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'' television series. He treated working on the show the same way he would work on a film.<ref name="Sizzle" /> When designing the [[droid]] [[B2EMO]], Scanlan and his team decided to design something that was rectangular and squat. They looked at the script and were able to understand what B2EMO would have to do in the show. The team considered this as well as the droid's relationship with the surrounding world, allowing them to figure out how to emote through small gestures, body language, and the motion of the head.<ref name="ProductionBrief">{{Getty|url=thewaltdisneystudios/allaccess#!asset/gppr5wpqgb4t74974f8s|text=ANDOR Production Brief V3 FINAL 8-04-22|author=[[Gina McIntyre|McIntyre, Gina]]|date=2022-08-04}}</ref> Scanlan and his creature shop built B2EMO from scratch, and they figured out every detail including his square figure and red color. The droid was entirely practical and controlled with a remote, allowing the actors to share scenes with the droid.<ref name="Meet B2EMO">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/tv/star-wars-andor-b2emo-droid|date=2022-09-14|text=Meet B2EMO, the adorable new salvage droid in Andor|author=Coggan, Devan|archivedate=20250217152503}}</ref> B2EMO was the first droid built by Scanlan's team that was able to do things that could be recognized emotionally, and he was capable of shrinking down.<ref name="ProductionBrief" />

